    38	| Existing same-key version | Persistence begins after any Brief version already exists for the key | Return and stamp the latest same-key version without publishing candidates | No project-baseline retry is needed |
    39	| No same-key version, stale project baseline | Another Brief with different inputs became newest after baseline pinning | Preserve the current `null` return so `publishDerivedBrief` rereads and retries | No rows or generation stamp are written |
